  },
  "script": "I've walked the Menlung Glacier in Nepal. In 1951, the climber Eric Shipton photographed a giant footprint there, with an ice axe next to it for scale. That one photo made the yeti famous. In 2017, scientists finally tested nine yeti samples from museums and monasteries. Bones, teeth, hair, skin. Eight came from bears. One came from a dog. I still stop at every track in the snow, though."
 },
